# The realism suite (Amendment T §3.3): the generated Earth at matched biomes, scales and
# light, rendered at every audit and laid beside photographs of real places of the same kind
# (`bench realism photos`, `docs/review/realism/references.md`) and measured
# (`bench realism images`). Scales: the ground underfoot (cm–1 m), the site at eye height
# (1–100 m), a slope from a rise of 40 m (10 m–1 km), the view from a hill 400 m up (1–10 km).
# Light: late morning, and a low sun in the early morning (pitch: degrees below the horizon).
# Kept as JPEGs in docs/review/realism/suite/.
# `hearth --game-dir DIR --software --screenshot-list tools/shots/realism.shots`
defaults: seed=7, planet=earth, res=2048, w=960, h=540, fov=60, dist=6, lod=256, season=summer, yaw=30, dry=true
